     1	# Literal invocation environment
     2	
     3	`CommandInvokeOptions.replaceEnv?: boolean` is additive. Absent or false retains
     4	the runtime's existing environment merge behavior and PWD treatment. True uses
     5	a fresh copy of exactly `options.env ?? {}` as the exported environment at
     6	command entry: no merge with inherited exports, implicit PWD or promotion of
     7	unexported/local variables. Supplied PWD is an environment value, not a cwd setter.
     8	Environment key/value validation remains required before child execution.
     9	
    10	This replaces the child environment, not generic shell state. Parent values,
    11	export attributes and function locals must remain unchanged on success, error
    12	or cancellation. Cwd resolution remains independent. A child Bash interpreter's
    13	own initialization is separate from the environment passed to it.
    14	
    15	Literal argv, middleware, shared execution/output/depth budgets, signal,
    16	stdout/stderr transfer and stdin cursor/origin rules are unchanged. Do not
    17	implement replacement with a new Shell, new budget or a callback-only bypass.
    18	
    19	Core `env COMMAND` explicitly requests replacement for its already-computed
    20	environment, including plain assignments and `-u`, not just `-i`. With no invoke
    21	hook, its existing registry/callback fallback still receives that exact map.
    22	Generic directExecutor/xargs/find callers retain their existing default behavior.
    23	
    24	Curie owns the contract/core consumer; Sagan owns runtime/types. The additive
    25	field and boundary-forwarding tests do not establish runtime support. Acceptance
    26	requires the actual-shell nested env row and export/local/parent/cancellation
    27	regressions after both implementations are committed. Preserve the historical
    28	leak reproduction and original six-row cohort.
